  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "The ninth inning broke a game that never trailed before it.",
    "what_this_means": "McNeil walked it off with a single after the Athletics had led wire-to-wire but let Toronto claw back into it. They didn't fold. They executed the late moment that mattered most. A clutch role player converting runners already in scoring position into a walk-off at-bat, the kind of small-margin win this offense has learned to take. The bullpen held it together after Lopez exited. Medina pitched 1.2 scoreless, Harris surrendered one in the eighth but the lead survived. This is becoming their pattern: lead early, stay ahead, finish it late when someone hits. That formula only works when the closer's available and fresh.",
